# Olie api-main (Cursor)

## Sources of truth

- `AGENTS.md` — Laravel Boost baseline (always follow)
- `.ai/guidelines/*` — project conventions (composed into AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md)
- `.ai/rules/index.md` — **read before planning/editing**; load matching rule files
- `.ai/skills/*` and `.cursor/skills/*` — activate on-demand for the domain
- `docs/concepts/*` — RoleType, soft-delete/cascade, feature flags

`CLAUDE.md` is the Claude Code entrypoint; Cursor should prefer `AGENTS.md` + `.ai/`. Where they disagree on **this** codebase, `.ai/` and `CLAUDE.md` project sections win over generic Boost text.

## Runtime

All PHP/Artisan/Composer/Pint/tests:

`docker exec olie-api-main <command>`

Do not run bare `php artisan` on the host.

## Non-negotiables

1. Scope by `frame_id` / `FrameContext` — never leak across tenants
2. Throw `BaseException` subclasses — never hand-build error JSON
3. Permissions only via `PermissionsSeeder` + seeder-running migration
4. Tests required; cancel if they cannot run
5. No AI co-author trailers on commits/PRs; PR body in pt-BR

## Boost MCP

Prefer Laravel Boost MCP tools (`search-docs`, `database-schema`, `database-query`, `record-rule`, …) over ad-hoc shell. Record durable conventions with `record-rule`, not personal memory.
